/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter/deployments","created_at":"2020-04-18T15:24:10Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T09:26:09Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-11T10:09:01Z","git_url":"git://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter","homepage":"","size":8329,"stargazers_count":12916,"watchers_count":12916,"language":"Tree-sitter Query","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":1065,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":280,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["hacktoberfest","neovim","nvim-treesitter","tree-sitter"],"visibility":"public","forks":1065,"open_issues":280,"watchers":12916,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"### Describe the bug\r\n\r\nWhen you write too much -> in a single expression, the C TreeSitter segfaults. When I say \"too much\", it's like 20.\r\n\r\n### To Reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Open a file with the C TreeSitter enabled\r\n2. Copy the following text : \r\n```{c}\r\n#include <stdio.h>\r\n\r\nstruct LinkedList {\r\n\tchar info[50];\r\n\tstruct LinkedList *next;\r\n};\r\n\r\nint main() {\r\n\tstruct LinkedList head = {\"heeyyyyyy\", NULL};\r\n\thead.next = &head;\r\n\r\n\tputs(head.next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next-next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next-next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next-next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->next->info);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n3. Observe NeoVim segfaulting\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThe TreeSitter not segfaulting and managing to highlight the text.\r\n\r\n### Output of `:checkhealth nvim-treesitter`\r\n\r\n```markdown\r\nnvim-treesitter: require(\"nvim-treesitter.health\").check()\r\n========================================================================\r\n## Installation\r\n  - OK: `tree-sitter` found 0.20.6 (parser generator, only needed for :\r\n  TSInstallFromGrammar)\r\n  - WARNING: `node` executable not found (only needed for :TSInstallFromGrammar,\r\n  not required for :TSInstall)\r\n  - OK: `git` executable found.\r\n  - OK: `cc` executable found. Selected from { vim.NIL, \"cc\", \"gcc\", \"clang\",\r\n  \"cl\", \"zig\" }\r\n    Version: cc (GCC) 11.2.0\r\n  - OK: Neovim was compiled with tree-sitter runtime ABI version 14 (required\r\n  >=13). Parsers must be compatible with runtime ABI.\r\n\r\n## Parser/Features H L F I J\r\n  - cpp            ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓\r\n  - rust           ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓\r\n  - markdown       ✓ . ✓ . ✓\r\n  - jsonc          ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓\r\n  - c              ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓ ✓\r\n\r\n  Legend: H[ighlight], L[ocals], F[olds], I[ndents], In[j]ections\r\n         +) multiple parsers found, only one will be used\r\n         x) errors found in the query, try to run :TS